# Vulnerability exceptions for the svcdoctor OCI image.
#
# ADR 0062 section 19: the release gate blocks on HIGH and CRITICAL findings.
# A finding may be released past only with a written justification that names
# the CVE and explains why it is not reachable in the shipped runtime — and that
# justification belongs here and in the release notes, not in a scanner flag.
#
# This file is deliberately empty of entries.
#
# What it must never become: a way to make the gate quiet. `--ignore-unfixed`
# and a blanket severity downgrade were both rejected in Phase 7.1-R for the
# same reason — a gate nobody can fail is not a gate. Each line added here is a
# decision someone made and signed their name to in review.
#
# Format, when an entry is genuinely needed:
#
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN
#   # <date> <who reviewed it>
#   # Why it is not reachable: the image contains no shell and no package
#   # manager, and nothing in svcdoctor executes <component>. The package is
#   # present only because <base image reason>.
#   # Revisit when: <condition>
#
# Phase 7.1 measured 0 CRITICAL and 0 HIGH across 5 base OS packages and 3 Go
# components. That was one measurement of one image, not a promise about future
# CVEs — which is exactly why this file exists rather than an assumption that it
# never will.
